.TH CHTTPCLIENT_SET_POOL_SIZE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_set_pool_size \- set the connection pool size
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_set_pool_size(chttpcli cli, size_t n);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Sets the maximum number of concurrent in-flight requests.  Callers
that call chttpclient_do when the limit is reached will block until
one becomes free.

Passing 0 selects the CPU count (the default).

May be called before or after the client has issued any requests, and
takes effect immediately (broadcasting to wake any blocked callers if
the limit grew).  This is purely a concurrency cap; it is unrelated to
the separate keep-alive idle-connection cache, which has its own
internal, fixed per-origin and total caps.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli   Client handle; must not be NULL.
n     Pool size; 0 = CPU count.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success            Pool size updated.
ccol_invalid_args       cli is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR create_chttpclient (3),
.BR chttpclient_do (3)
